00:00:00.061 --> 00:00:00.898
- Oh! Oh! He wrote back!

00:00:00.898 --> 00:00:01.978
He wrote back!

00:00:01.978 --> 00:00:02.733
He wrote back!

00:00:06.011 --> 00:00:08.462
- I've been with my wife
for about ten years.

00:00:08.462 --> 00:00:10.122
- I've been married for seven years.

00:00:10.122 --> 00:00:12.060
- We met because we lived in the same dorm

00:00:12.060 --> 00:00:13.135
freshman year of college.

00:00:13.135 --> 00:00:15.295
- I've been married for
about two and a half years.

00:00:15.295 --> 00:00:17.466
- We were set up by my best friend

00:00:17.466 --> 00:00:18.847
who married us.

00:00:18.847 --> 00:00:21.412
- I've never once used a
dating app in my entire life.

00:00:21.412 --> 00:00:24.188
- Dating apps didn't
exist when I was single.

00:00:24.188 --> 00:00:26.311
- OkCupid was a thing
when I was in college,

00:00:26.311 --> 00:00:28.227
but it was kind of like

00:00:28.227 --> 00:00:30.189
there was a certain type of person

00:00:30.189 --> 00:00:31.687
who online-dated at that point.

00:00:31.687 --> 00:00:33.451
- I don't even know if
I've ever been on a date.

00:00:33.451 --> 00:00:34.472
- Tinder scares me.

00:00:34.472 --> 00:00:37.166
It feels a little shallow and judgemental.

00:00:37.166 --> 00:00:39.024
- So I'm putting on
Tinder for the first time.

00:00:39.024 --> 00:00:39.964
- Which way do I swipe?

00:00:39.964 --> 00:00:42.402
- The first person on my
Tinder is saucy as hell!

00:00:42.402 --> 00:00:43.481
- Definitely not!

00:00:43.481 --> 00:00:45.084
Griffin?

00:00:45.084 --> 00:00:46.546
- Oh! Oh! It's a match!

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.603
It's a match!

00:00:47.603 --> 00:00:48.171
Oh boy!

00:00:48.171 --> 00:00:49.448
Okay, wait!

00:00:49.448 --> 00:00:50.865
Do I send him a message?

00:00:50.865 --> 00:00:52.304
- This is you with your mother.

00:00:52.304 --> 00:00:53.871
- This is actually just like a video game

00:00:53.871 --> 00:00:54.847
and it's really fun.

00:00:54.847 --> 00:00:56.693
- Oo, gosh! I just got a match!

00:00:56.693 --> 00:00:57.876
What the hell does that mean?

00:00:57.876 --> 00:00:59.095
- Super like Ryan?

00:00:59.095 --> 00:01:00.953
No! No!

00:01:00.953 --> 00:01:04.471
- Is it weird to send
like multiple messages

00:01:04.471 --> 00:01:05.190
to a stranger?

00:01:05.190 --> 00:01:06.990
Like I just messaged three times in a row.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:09.706
- My second photo is a photo
taken on my wedding day.

00:01:09.706 --> 00:01:11.692
(laughs)

00:01:11.692 --> 00:01:13.498
Hopefully no one swipes to that photo.

00:01:13.498 --> 00:01:14.299
(laughs)

00:01:14.299 --> 00:01:15.738
- He's looking for fun, friendship,

00:01:15.738 --> 00:01:18.257
and possibly a greencard,
like that's funny!

00:01:18.257 --> 00:01:20.161
- I don't know which one this guy is!

00:01:20.161 --> 00:01:21.879
There are like eight
people in this profile.

00:01:21.879 --> 00:01:23.504
- If I was on Tinder, my
bio would be just like--

00:01:23.504 --> 00:01:25.942
just a string of eggplant emojis.

00:01:25.942 --> 00:01:27.440
Just straightforward.

00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:29.042
- I think that a lot of these men on here

00:01:29.042 --> 00:01:31.399
are confused as to what
is attractive to women.

00:01:31.399 --> 00:01:33.976
- Tinder was really fun,
but I feel like as soon

00:01:33.976 --> 00:01:36.681
as I get a response back,
then it's going to be like

00:01:36.681 --> 00:01:37.877
really daunting and scary.

00:01:37.877 --> 00:01:41.823
- I feel weird game-ifying
something that could be real.

00:01:41.823 --> 00:01:43.479
- If I was single, I would
definitely use Tinder.

00:01:43.479 --> 00:01:44.582
- I actually think it'd be something fun

00:01:44.582 --> 00:01:46.707
for my husband and I to play together

00:01:46.707 --> 00:01:48.947
as like a judging people sort of thing.

00:01:48.947 --> 00:01:50.783
- Being married fucking rules!

00:01:55.931 --> 00:01:57.289
- It does feel like there's a bunch

00:01:57.289 --> 00:01:58.949
of wonderful people here.

00:01:58.949 --> 00:02:00.086
Can I just have a Tinder for friends?

00:02:00.086 --> 00:02:00.567
I want to meet!

00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:01.318
I want to hang out!

00:02:01.318 --> 00:02:02.635
I'll bring my wife!

